{"page":205,"verses":[{"verse_key":"9:112","surah":9,"ayah":112,"ar_uthmani":"ٱلتَّـٰٓئِبُونَ ٱلْعَـٰبِدُونَ ٱلْحَـٰمِدُونَ ٱلسَّـٰٓئِحُونَ ٱلرَّٰكِعُونَ ٱلسَّـٰجِدُونَ ٱلْـَٔامِرُونَ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ وَٱلنَّاهُونَ عَنِ ٱلْمُنكَرِ وَٱلْحَـٰفِظُونَ لِحُدُودِ ٱللَّهِ ۗ وَبَشِّرِ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"[The believers are] those who turn to God in repentance; who worship and praise Him; who fast, bow down and prostrate themselves; who order what is good, forbid what is wrong and observe God’s limits. Give glad news to such believers.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"ٱلتَّـٰٓئِبُونَ","en_gloss":"Those who turn in repentance","transliteration":"al-tāibūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلْعَـٰبِدُونَ","en_gloss":"those who worship","transliteration":"l-ʿābidūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلْحَـٰمِدُونَ","en_gloss":"those who praise","transliteration":"l-ḥāmidūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":4,"ar":"ٱلسَّـٰٓئِحُونَ","en_gloss":"those who go out","transliteration":"l-sāiḥūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلرَّٰكِعُونَ","en_gloss":"those who bow down","transliteration":"l-rākiʿūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلسَّـٰجِدُونَ","en_gloss":"those who prostrate","transliteration":"l-sājidūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱلْـَٔامِرُونَ","en_gloss":"those who enjoin","transliteration":"l-āmirūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":8,"ar":"بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ","en_gloss":"the right","transliteration":"bil-maʿrūfi","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَٱلنَّاهُونَ","en_gloss":"and those who forbid","transliteration":"wal-nāhūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":10,"ar":"عَنِ","en_gloss":"[on]","transliteration":"ʿani","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱلْمُنكَرِ","en_gloss":"the wrong","transliteration":"l-munkari","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَٱلْحَـٰفِظُونَ","en_gloss":"and those who observe","transliteration":"wal-ḥāfiẓūna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":13,"ar":"لِحُدُودِ","en_gloss":"(the) limits","transliteration":"liḥudūdi","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":14,"ar":"ٱللَّهِ ۗ","en_gloss":"(of) Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":15,"ar":"وَبَشِّرِ","en_gloss":"And give glad tidings","transliteration":"wabashiri","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":16,"ar":"ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","en_gloss":"(to) the believers","transliteration":"l-mu'minīna","verse_key":"9:112"},{"pos":17,"ar":"١١٢","en_gloss":"(112)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"9:112"}]},{"verse_key":"9:113","surah":9,"ayah":113,"ar_uthmani":"مَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِىِّ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ أَن يَسْتَغْفِرُوا۟ لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ وَلَوْ كَانُوٓا۟ أُو۟لِى قُرْبَىٰ مِنۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ أَنَّهُمْ أَصْحَـٰبُ ٱلْجَحِيمِ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"It is not fitting for the Prophet and the believers to ask forgiveness for the idolaters- even if they are related to them- after having been shown that they are the inhabitants of the Blaze:","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"Not","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":2,"ar":"كَانَ","en_gloss":"(it) is","transliteration":"kāna","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":3,"ar":"لِلنَّبِىِّ","en_gloss":"for the Prophet","transliteration":"lilnnabiyyi","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":4,"ar":"وَٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"and those who","transliteration":"wa-alladhīna","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ءَامَنُوٓا۟","en_gloss":"believe","transliteration":"āmanū","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":6,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"that","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":7,"ar":"يَسْتَغْفِرُوا۟","en_gloss":"they ask forgiveness","transliteration":"yastaghfirū","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":8,"ar":"لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ","en_gloss":"for the polytheists","transliteration":"lil'mush'rikīna","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَلَوْ","en_gloss":"even though","transliteration":"walaw","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":10,"ar":"كَانُوٓا۟","en_gloss":"they be","transliteration":"kānū","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":11,"ar":"أُو۟لِى","en_gloss":"near of kin","transliteration":"ulī","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":12,"ar":"قُرْبَىٰ","en_gloss":"near of kin","transliteration":"qur'bā","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":13,"ar":"مِنۢ","en_gloss":"after","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":14,"ar":"بَعْدِ","en_gloss":"after","transliteration":"baʿdi","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":15,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"[what]","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":16,"ar":"تَبَيَّنَ","en_gloss":"has become clear","transliteration":"tabayyana","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":17,"ar":"لَهُمْ","en_gloss":"to them","transliteration":"lahum","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":18,"ar":"أَنَّهُمْ","en_gloss":"that they","transliteration":"annahum","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":19,"ar":"أَصْحَـٰبُ","en_gloss":"(are the) companions","transliteration":"aṣḥābu","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":20,"ar":"ٱلْجَحِيمِ","en_gloss":"(of) the Hellfire","transliteration":"l-jaḥīmi","verse_key":"9:113"},{"pos":21,"ar":"١١٣","en_gloss":"(113)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"9:113"}]},{"verse_key":"9:114","surah":9,"ayah":114,"ar_uthmani":"وَمَا كَانَ ٱسْتِغْفَارُ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ لِأَبِيهِ إِلَّا عَن مَّوْعِدَةٍ وَعَدَهَآ إِيَّاهُ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُۥٓ أَنَّهُۥ عَدُوٌّ لِّلَّهِ تَبَرَّأَ مِنْهُ ۚ إِنَّ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ لَأَوَّٰهٌ حَلِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Abraham asked forgiveness for his father because he had made a promise to him, but once he realized that his father was an enemy of God, he washed his hands of him. Abraham was tender-hearted and forbearing.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَمَا","en_gloss":"And not","transliteration":"wamā","verse_key":"9:114"},{"pos":2,"ar":"كَانَ","en_gloss":"was","transliteration":"kāna","verse_key":"9:114"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱسْتِغْفَارُ","en_gloss":"(the) asking of forgiveness","transliteration":"is'tigh'fāru","verse_key":"9:114"},{"pos":4,"ar":"إِبْرَٰهِيمَ","en_gloss":"(by) Ibrahim","transliteration":"ib'rāhīma","verse_key":"9:114"},{"pos":5,"ar":"لِأَبِيهِ","en_gloss":"for his father","transliteration":"li-abīhi","verse_key":"9:114"},{"pos":6,"ar":"إِلَّا","en_gloss":"except